gosh seam 18: The core's utilities are a domain, Util: its ABI at the top of src/util, its sources under imp/.

For:   REQ22/SHAPE-1, the core factored into domains by the seam, its utilities after its
       programs. The lint holds it (seam/DOMAINS). Until now nothing of it was in a namespace, so a
       use of it could not be told from a name: Select, swrite, the frozen timestamp and the
       locale's helpers were the program's, as every name in no namespace is.
What:  Moves, and renames of where names are, and nothing else: no byte of the protocol, and no
       behaviour, changes. Its sources are moved under src/util/imp/ by git's renames. What its
       headers declare is in Util: Select, swrite, freeze_timestamp and frozen_timestamp,
       LocaleVar and the locale's functions, and the two functions behind fatal_assert and
       dos_assert, which the macros now call as Util::. The macros keep their names (a macro is
       in no namespace), and so do pty_compat's my_forkpty and my_cfmakeraw, which stand for the
       system's own where a system lacks them (seam/DOMAINS allows them). Their users say Util::.
Where: src/util/ (Makefile.am, every header; imp/); the users of its names in src/frontend,
       src/network, src/examples and src/tests.
Kind:  five files moved; the names of six headers in Util; their users qualified.
From:  the core at the pin: src/util/{locale_utils.cc,pty_compat.cc,select.cc,swrite.cc,timestamp.cc}.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

